  "result": "Perfect! All 256 tests pass (236 existing + 20 new overdue invoice tests).\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n\u2705 **src/reports.js** \u2014 New module for reporting:\n- `overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)` function\n  - Filters invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n  - Filters for dueDate strictly before asOf\n  - Returns ok([...]) with array of overdue invoices\n  - Each record: { number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }\n  - daysOverdue calculated via daysBetween(dueDate, asOf)\n  - due calculated via balanceDue(invoice)\n  - Sorted by daysOverdue descending (most overdue first)\n  - Validates asOf date (DATE_INVALID for invalid)\n\n\u2705 **test/reports.test.js** \u2014 20 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Filtering by status (issued/partially_paid)\n- Excluding draft/paid invoices\n- Excluding invoices with dueDate equal to or after asOf\n- Correct daysOverdue calculation\n- Sorting by most overdue first\n- DATE_INVALID validation\n- Field accuracy (number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due)\n- Invoices with payments\n- Complex invoices (discount, VAT, voucher)\n- Mixed statuses\n- No mutation\n- Different customers and edge cases\n\nAll implementations follow house rules: integer cents, fail() pattern for errors, immutable transformations, and comprehensive test coverage.",
